## Codex Review (GPT-5.5)
Reviewed the full PR branch against freshly fetched `upstream/master`. Dominant PR type: feature, with public API, docs, and tests as secondary scope.

### 1. Bugs / Issues

#### 1. 🔴 Disabled text controls can receive synthetic clicks (blocking)

`Drawer.VirtualKeyboardProvider` treats disabled text inputs/textareas as keyboard targets, then prevents the native `touchend` and dispatches its own click. Real taps on a disabled input emit touch events but do not produce a native click; this path can make disabled controls run `onClick` handlers anyway.

`packages/react/src/drawer/virtual-keyboard-provider/DrawerVirtualKeyboardProvider.tsx`

```ts
return element instanceof win.HTMLInputElement && KEYBOARD_INPUT_TYPES.has(element.type);
```

```ts
event.preventDefault();
focusKeyboardInputWithoutPageScroll(keyboardFocusTarget);
dispatchKeyboardClick(keyboardClickTarget, touch);
```

**Fix:** Exclude disabled keyboard controls from `isKeyboardInputElement`, preferably using the platform disabled state (`:disabled` or the relevant form-control `disabled` checks), and add coverage for disabled input/textarea and disabled labelled-control taps.

#### 2. 🔴 Shadow-root inputs lose scroll slack/alignment (blocking)

The provider can detect a focused input through a shadow root, but scroll-target lookup starts from `target.parentElement` and `findScrollableTouchTarget` also walks via `parentElement`. For an input inside a shadow root, that traversal stops at the shadow boundary, so the provider can set `--drawer-keyboard-inset` but cannot find the drawer body scroller to add slack or align the field above the keyboard.

`packages/react/src/drawer/virtual-keyboard-provider/DrawerVirtualKeyboardProvider.tsx`

```ts
return (
  findScrollableTouchTarget(target.parentElement, root, 'vertical') ??
  findScrollableTouchTarget(target.parentElement, root, 'vertical', true)
);
```

`packages/react/src/utils/scrollable.ts`

```ts
while (node && node !== root) {
  if (isScrollable(node, axis, allowOverflowIntent)) {
    return node;
  }
  node = node.parentElement;
}
```

**Fix:** Use composed-tree ancestor traversal for scroll target discovery so it can cross slots/shadow hosts, and add a browser test where a shadow-root input inside a scrollable drawer content receives slack and scroll alignment.

### Test Coverage Assessment

I ran `pnpm test:chromium DrawerVirtualKeyboardProvider --no-watch` and `pnpm test:chromium DrawerViewport --no-watch`; both passed. I did not verify the new regression tests fail on `upstream/master`.

### Recommendation

Request changes 🔴

The new provider is a public interaction API, and both issues affect core tap/focus/scroll behavior. I’d fix these before shipping it.
